flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the drive<br/>amplifier heatsink fins for dust or blocked<br/>ventilation slots. 2. Check the motor body for<br/>abnormal surface temperature with a contact<br/>thermometer. 3. Inspect the drive amplifier display<br/>for thermal warning or fault codes."]
    box_2["Hold a calibrated infrared thermometer or a contact<br/>thermocouple probe against the drive amplifier<br/>heatsink surface after the axis has been running<br/>under normal load for 20 minutes. Record the<br/>heatsink temperature and compare against the maximum<br/>permitted heatsink temperature stated in the drive<br/>amplifier datasheet. An overtemperature condition<br/>with normal ambient temperature indicates a failed<br/>cooling fan or blocked heatsink fins."]
    box_3[/"Refer to the drive thermal derating limits."/]
    box_4{"Drive heatsink temperature within rated continuous<br/>limit?"}
    box_5(["End, Escalate: drive overtemperature, check cabinet<br/>cooling"])
    box_6["Isolate the motor from the drive amplifier at the<br/>motor terminal block. Using a calibrated megohmeter<br/>set to 500 volts DC, measure insulation resistance<br/>phase to phase and phase to earth on all three motor<br/>windings. Record all six readings and compare<br/>against the minimum insulation resistance of 1<br/>megaohm for a motor in service; any reading below<br/>this limit requires motor withdrawal for inspection."]
    box_7{"Winding resistance balanced within 2% across all<br/>phases?"}
    box_8["Inspect motor terminal block, tighten connections,<br/>check insulation"]
    box_9["Inspect the encoder read head status indicator light<br/>on the motor body or drive amplifier; green<br/>indicates a valid signal and red or flashing<br/>indicates a fault. Check the encoder cable<br/>continuity at both the motor connector and the drive<br/>connector using a continuity tester on each signal<br/>wire. Inspect the cable route for crush damage,<br/>sharp bends, or contact with hot or moving surfaces."]
    box_10{"Encoder hardware status normal, no fault flags in<br/>drive?"}
    box_11(["End, Replace encoder: hardware fault confirmed"])
    box_12["Command the axis to traverse at three test speeds<br/>covering 10%, 50%, and 90% of rapid traverse rate<br/>using the machine diagnostic mode. At each speed,<br/>read the following error value from the drive<br/>diagnostic display or the CNC parameter screen.<br/>Record the following error in encoder counts and<br/>compare against the maximum following error limit<br/>programmed in the drive parameters."]
    box_13[/"Refer to the following error specification."/]
    box_14{"Following error within specified limit at all three<br/>speeds?"}
    box_15["Adjust servo gain parameters, Kp, Ki within drive<br/>tuning limits"]
    box_16{"Reverify following error after gain adjustment"}
    box_17(["End, Escalate: following error persistent,<br/>mechanical load check required"])
    box_18["Command the axis to move to each of ten programmed<br/>reference positions distributed across the full<br/>working travel using the machine diagnostic<br/>positioning cycle. At each position, read the<br/>position feedback value from the controller display<br/>and subtract the commanded position to obtain the<br/>position error. Record all ten errors and compare<br/>the maximum absolute error against the axis<br/>positioning accuracy specification."]
    box_19[/"Refer to the axis position accuracy specification."/]
    box_20{"Position accuracy within ±0.005 mm at all reference<br/>positions?"}
    box_21["Complete the following steps: 1. Access the encoder<br/>calibration menu via the service laptop. 2. Select<br/>the encoder calibration routine and follow the on-<br/>screen procedure. 3. Record the calibration result<br/>and confirm the residual error is within tolerance."]
    box_22{"Reverify position accuracy after encoder<br/>recalibration"}
    box_23(["End, Escalate: position accuracy unrecoverable,<br/>geometric check required"])
    box_24["With the motor power on and the brake released,<br/>command the axis to a mid travel position. Switch<br/>the brake on by de energising the brake coil and<br/>attempt to push the axis by hand in both directions.<br/>Attach a torque wrench to the motor shaft coupling<br/>and measure the holding torque; compare against the<br/>minimum rated brake torque in the motor datasheet."]
    box_25[/"Refer to the motor brake specification."/]
    box_26{"Brake holding torque within rated value?"}
    box_27["Replace motor brake or adjust air gap"]
    box_28["Mount a dial test indicator against the axis slide<br/>with the probe oriented along the axis direction.<br/>Command a series of small reversals across a 5<br/>millimetre range at slow feed rate. Read the<br/>indicator displacement at each reversal and record<br/>the maximum lost motion observed. Compare against<br/>the maximum permitted backlash value in the axis<br/>specification; if exceeded the ballscrew nut preload<br/>requires adjustment or replacement."]
    box_29{"Axis backlash within 0.008 mm limit?"}
    box_30["Adjust coupling preload or replace worn coupling<br/>element"]
    box_31["Command the axis to run continuously at rated speed<br/>for one minute while recording the velocity feedback<br/>signal from the drive diagnostic output. Perform a<br/>frequency spectrum analysis on the velocity trace<br/>using the drive oscilloscope function or external<br/>data acquisition. Identify any peak above 5% of the<br/>mean velocity in the 10 to 500 hertz range and<br/>compare against the baseline spectrum recorded<br/>during the previous service."]
    box_32{"No significant harmonic peaks in velocity frequency<br/>spectrum?"}
    box_33["Investigate speed ripple source, bearing or encoder<br/>pitch error"]
    box_34["Log all drive parameters and test data"]
    box_35["Update drive parameter backup and maintenance<br/>management system service record"]
    box_36(["End, Procedure complete"])
    box_37["Secondary servo tuning attempt: access the drive<br/>parameter menu and increase the proportional<br/>velocity gain by 10% of its current value. Command a<br/>positioning move and read the following error value<br/>at the same three test speeds. If the error<br/>increases at any speed, restore the original gain<br/>value and note that mechanical resonance may be<br/>contributing, requiring a drive frequency spectrum<br/>analysis before returning to the following error<br/>measurement step."]
    box_38[/"Encoder signal diagnostic (GRAPH 35)"/]

